kevin_prod: Heads up — small team onboarding from Node. During warmup we saw a big spike of 429s and some auth failures. ~200 parallel clients for a brief ramp. Logs show `insufficient_quota` then lots of 429s. Anyone seen this pattern?

sam_cs: Hi @kevin_prod — can you paste the tiny init snippet + the raw error lines? Two quick Qs: are you preflighting per tab/client or reusing per process? And are tokens ephemeral per-request?

kevin_prod: Logs:
```
[2026-03-23T14:12:03Z] client=svc-a auth=ok token_age=3s req_id=ab12 status=200
[2026-03-23T14:12:03Z] client=svc-b auth=failed error=insufficient_quota rev=1
[2026-03-23T14:12:03Z] client=svc-c status=429 message="rate limit exceeded"
```
Init:
```
const sdk = new Redwood({ apiKey: process.env.RW_KEY });
await sdk.preflight(); // called on every user session open
```
We were following quickstart and ended up preflighting a lot.

sam_cs: Ok that explains it. Quick mitigation: stop calling full preflight on every session. Cache the result for 30–60s per process. Also splay the warmup across clients instead of doing 200 concurrent preflights.

ahmad_eng: Infra notes: we saw the burst come from ~80 source IPs at the same timestamp. Our onboarding guardrails throttle preflight-heavy patterns to protect shared capacity. For immediate fixes: reuse ephemeral tokens across a session instead of creating one per request; limit preflight concurrency to <=20 during ramp; enable http2 keepalive/connection reuse to reduce overhead.

ahmad_eng: Example changes to add on your side:
```
// cache preflight for 45s per process
let _pf = null;
async function cachedPreflight() {
  if (_pf && Date.now() - _pf.ts < 45000) return _pf.res;
  const res = await sdk.preflight();
  _pf = { ts: Date.now(), res };
  return res;
}
// splay before heavy ops
const jitter = Math.floor(Math.random()*300)+50; // 50-350ms
await sleep(jitter);
await cachedPreflight();
```
That pattern usually collapses the stampede.

onboard-bot: Rate alert: key=rw_live_•••• saw 429 spike at 2026-03-23T14:12:00Z. Window=120s, peak_rps=52, avg_rps=11. Recommend lower concurrency.

kevin_prod: Implemented patch: cached preflight 45s, splay, reduced warmup parallelism to 15. Quick canary shows 429s dropped from ~30% sessions -> ~1-2%.

sam_cs: Great. Two follow-ups: 1) we'll open a short support ticket if you need a temporary warmup whitelist for >20 concurrency. 2) please share your final deploy time so CS/ops can correlate logs and lift temporary throttles if requested. Docs: https://docs.redwood.ai/onboarding/preflight-best-practices

ahmad_eng: If you expect sustained >50 rps we can discuss Dedicated warmup or temporary per-key quota increase for ~10 minutes. For now the client changes should be sufficient.

kevin_prod: Will run gradual ramp with the cached preflight and splay. Filing the ticket now and will paste the id here. Thanks all :raised_hands:
